{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789343057,"nonce":"qVlunXe2CgTnfMnyNC4ru5ftYrI=","title":"zypy compiles a ten-line program in 45 ms","message":"`compile_typed_program` for `bench_fib.py` (fib and main, 486\ndeclarations counting the builtins library), sampled over 400 compiles:\n\n    lower_typed_program        32%   of which cloning the whole prelowered\n                                     library into the program's module\n                                     (422 functions) and dropping the 350\n                                     unreachable ones again is about half;\n                                     lowering the 30 exception-class\n                                     functions the prelude generates is\n                                     most of the rest\n    run_interp_safe_opts       20%   every pass walking the 33 library\n                                     functions again; drop_insert's facts\n                                     and inline's callee snapshot lead\n    Cranelift                  20%   72 functions, 3659 instructions, of\n                                     which the exception classes' new/\n                                     unbox/init and the dynamic repr family\n                                     reached from the uncaught-exception\n                                     printer are about 60\n    reachability, retain        6%\n    parse + inference + Python lowering: 0.45 ms\n\nTwo things done here, 44 to 28 ms:\n\n* A prelowered module is adopted as it is reached: the linker copies in\n  a function when a body calls it, and its callees in turn, instead of\n  the whole module (lowering.rs `adopt_prelowered_reached`). A program\n  with no entry point still adopts everything.\n* A function already through the pipeline is left alone\n  (`FunctionAttributes::optimized`, set on a snapshot's functions after\n  its own passes). Per-function passes skip it; box_reads clears it\n  where it expands, so the LICM/CSE that follow see the loads.\n\nWhat is left is structural:\n\n* The tiered runtime does not start in the interpreter. Tier 0 is\n  Cranelift, eagerly compiled for every reachable function at load\n  (`TieredBackend::compile_module_reaching`), and `hir_interp` is used\n  by the interp runtime only. So the exception constructors and the\n  repr family are compiled before the first call and never run. Lazy\n  per-function compilation through the reload cells, or a real\n  interpreter tier 0, would take the Cranelift share to what the program\n  executes.\n* The prelude exception classes are generated and lowered per program\n  (a440a60) because a class's `$unbox` accepts its subclasses by index;\n  moving them into the snapshot needs the subclass test to be a runtime\n  lookup.\n* drop_insert computes its module facts over every function each\n  compile; the snapshot's could be stored.\n* `ZYNTAX_TRACE_OPT_PHASES=1` now splits codegen into Cranelift and\n  registration.","files":null}]}